fact WorkItem(id: "WI-425", description: some(value: "Make Expr::DotApply's structural view ISOMORPHIC to its dot_apply term twin (kb/term_view.rs occ_head / occ_pos_child / occ_named_child / occ_named_keys). WI-397 made DotApply structural (was Opaque-by-omission) so a fact embedding a DotApply (a compound-projection receiver `s.cell`) indexes in the discrim tree. But the structural view is NOT isomorphic to the dot_apply TERM the loader emits: load.rs (LoadBuildFrame::DotApply ~5483) ALWAYS builds `dot_apply(receiver, name, args: List[ApplyArg])` — arity-3, with `args = nil` even for a field access `r.name` — whereas occ_head maps a FIELD-form DotApply to arity-2 `{name, receiver}` (no args) and a METHOD form rides its call args as positional/named children instead of the `args` List. So a DotApply OCCURRENCE and its dot_apply TERM twin produce DIFFERENT discrim keys (Functor dot_apply -> Arity 2-vs-3 -> different NamedKeys), violating node-carrier-mirrors-term-structure. LATENT today: nothing matches a DotApply occurrence against a dot_apply term in the discrim tree — the typer dot engine uses a dedicated hand-matcher (try_fire_dot_rule, typing.rs ~1823, NOT the generic view); op-bodies are not discrim-indexed as facts; try_occurrence_to_term has no DotApply arm, so an occurrence never co-lowers to the arity-3 twin in the same tree. WI-397 is self-consistent (its projection receiver is an OCCURRENCE indexed by occ_head, never matched against a TERM). But the divergence is a soundness landmine the moment any consumer crosses the two carriers (discrim-query-is-the-unifier: a missed cross-carrier match is a WRONG answer, not just a perf loss). FIX: make occ_head/occ_pos_child/occ_named_child/occ_named_keys mirror the dot_apply term EXACTLY — head `dot_apply`, named children `{receiver, name, args}` where `args` is the List[ApplyArg] synthesized from the Expr's pos_args+named_args (each wrapped as an ApplyArg with optional name, matching the loader's mk_apply_arg encoding) — so a DotApply occurrence reads byte-identically to its hash-consed dot_apply term via TermView. RELATED latent items from the WI-397 /code-review, SUBSUMED by this fix: (a) type_head now classifies a bare DotApply Node as Parameterized{base: dot_apply} (the named_arity>0 fallthrough in type_head, typing.rs) — harmless today (the projection eliminator reads the receiver via extract_sort_ref_sym, which returns None for a DotApply, then the explicit DotApply branch), but sort_functor_of_view(DotApply) returns Some(dot_apply), so a future consumer calling extract_type/sort_functor_of_view on a DotApply receiver would treat `dot_apply` as a real sort; (b) occ_head reports named_arity = 2 + named_args.len() unconditionally while occ_named_keys only emits `name`/`receiver` keys guarded by lookup_symbol — an invariant worth asserting (sound today: name/receiver are interned at prelude load before any DotApply fact insert). ACCEPTANCE: a DotApply occurrence and the dot_apply term built for the same `r.name(args)` produce identical TermView head/keys/children + identical discrim keys; a regression test indexes one carrier and queries with the other and matches; full anthill-core green. Rust-only (kb/term_view.rs). Surfaced by the WI-397 /code-review (high effort)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-12T11:26:44Z"))

